# Create work instruction (Neubond)

> **Scope note:** This rule is inherited from `Neubond-App-v2` and describes the Loop I device,
> firmware, and Flutter app QMS. Its paths (`docs/qms/`, `lib/`, `ios/`, `west.yml`) refer to those
> repositories, not this web app. Kept here for when the web app enters IEC 62304 scope.

When the user asks to **create work instruction**, **create wi**, **draft work instruction**, **write work instruction**, or similar:

Follow `.cursor/commands/create-work-instruction.md` in full.

Key points:

- Canonical template: `docs/qms/Templates/work_instruction_template.md`
- Cursor command: `.cursor/commands/create-work-instruction.md`
- Human guide: `docs/ops_guide/work_instruction_generation.md`
- Two procedure formats: **manufacturing** (parts + tools) vs **software / operations** (inputs + verification)
- Imperative steps with **Step N** / **N-M** numbering; **IQC:** blocks after inspectable steps
- Manufacturing parts: `NAME (LP1-XXX)` with `x1` / `2x` quantities
- Draft output: `docs/qms/work_instructions/<wi-number>_<slug>.md`
- Ops guides (`docs/ops_guide/`) are drafting inputs — approved WIs cite **NBD-LP1-*** controlled docs, not ops paths
- Respect **draft only** — chat output, no file write
- Do not commit unless explicitly asked
